      "text": "Cultures are always mixed and influenced by one another, so no culture has a pure or original form.",
      "value": 2,
      "rationale": "This is the core claim: Prashad aims to uncouple origins and authenticity from culture and Kelley calls cultures living and interacting.",
      "sources": [
        "s2",
        "s3"
      ],
      "addedAs": "unbroken-national-continuity"
    },
    {
      "text": "People's identities should be understood as drawing on many cultures rather than belonging to one group.",
      "value": 2,
      "rationale": "Kelley argues all people inherit European, African, Native American and Asian pasts and that polyculturalism means expanding who counts as Black.",
      "sources": [
        "s1",
        "s2"
      ],
      "declined": "Overlaps unbroken-national-continuity and no-fixed-category-of-women; not a distinct question."
    },
